{% doc %}
  Puts the first validation error on the next page.

  Settings is a column of small forms, so an error panel per form would
  mean rendering every form's state through the redirect. One message
  naming what went wrong, next to a screen that reopens where the admin
  was, says the same thing for far less machinery. If a form ever grows
  past a handful of fields this is the thing to replace.

  Returns true when it flashed something, so a caller can use it as the
  failure branch.

  @param {object} errors - A contract's errors, field name to messages
{% enddoc %}
{% liquid
  for field in errors
    for message in field[1]
      if message != blank
        function _ = 'modules/support/helpers/flash', message: message, severity: 'error'
        return true
      endif
    endfor
  endfor

  return false
%}
